{"seq":1,"slug":"climate-system-basics","title":"气候系统与能量平衡","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/natural-sciences/atmospheric-science/climate-and-climate-change/climate-system-basics","wordCount":1388,"readingTime":6,"html":"<h1 id=\"气候系统与能量平衡\">气候系统与能量平衡</h1><h2 id=\"知识要点\">知识要点</h2><p>天气和气候的区别，一句话我记了很久：&quot;天气决定你今天穿什么，气候决定你衣柜里有什么。&quot;天气是某一时刻的大气状态，气候是长期统计。这一节我们建立看待气候的整体框架。抓住：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>气候系统由五大圈层耦合组成，不止是大气；</li>\n<li>地球的能量收支：进出平衡决定全球平均温度；</li>\n<li>温室效应的物理本质——对短波透明、对长波部分吸收；</li>\n<li>反馈机制如何放大或抑制气候扰动。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>核心概念：气候系统、能量收支、行星反照率、温室效应、正反馈、负反馈。</p>\n<h2 id=\"详细讲解\">详细讲解</h2><h3 id=\"气候不只是大气\">气候不只是大气</h3><p>谈气候，不能只盯着空气。地球气候是五大圈层相互耦合的结果：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>圈层</th>\n<th>在气候中的角色</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>大气圈</td>\n<td>输送热量与水汽，变化最快</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>海洋圈</td>\n<td>巨大的热库，储存和搬运热量，变化慢</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>冰雪圈</td>\n<td>高反照率，反射阳光；融化会放大增暖</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>陆地圈</td>\n<td>影响反照率、水分与碳交换</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>生物圈</td>\n<td>参与碳循环，调节温室气体</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>这些圈层耦合在一起、时间尺度差异巨大，正是气候系统复杂而迷人的原因。海洋的&quot;慢&quot;也解释了为什么气候变化有滞后——即使排放停止，海洋的热惯性仍会让增暖持续一段时间。</p>\n<h3 id=\"地球的能量收支\">地球的能量收支</h3><p>全球平均温度，归根到底由一笔&quot;能量账&quot;决定：地球从太阳吸收多少短波辐射，又向太空放出多少长波辐射。长期平衡时，进出相等。</p>\n<p>进来的太阳辐射，一部分被云、冰雪、地表直接反射回太空，这个反射比例叫<strong>行星反照率</strong>，地球平均约 0.3，即约三成阳光被弹走。剩下被吸收的能量加热地表，地表再以长波（红外）辐射向外放热。</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"flowchart\" data-source=\"flowchart TB&#10;  S[&quot;太阳短波辐射进入&quot;] --&gt; R[&quot;约30% 被反照率反射回太空&quot;]&#10;  S --&gt; A[&quot;约70% 被地表与大气吸收&quot;]&#10;  A --&gt; E[&quot;地表发出长波红外辐射&quot;]&#10;  E --&gt; G[&quot;温室气体吸收部分长波&lt;br/&gt;再向下回辐射&quot;]&#10;  G --&gt; W[&quot;地表比无温室时更暖&quot;]\">flowchart TB\n  S[\"太阳短波辐射进入\"] --&gt; R[\"约30% 被反照率反射回太空\"]\n  S --&gt; A[\"约70% 被地表与大气吸收\"]\n  A --&gt; E[\"地表发出长波红外辐射\"]\n  E --&gt; G[\"温室气体吸收部分长波&lt;br/&gt;再向下回辐射\"]\n  G --&gt; W[\"地表比无温室时更暖\"]</pre><p>可以用一个最简能量平衡估算无大气时的地表温度。令吸收的太阳辐射等于地球以黑体方式放出的辐射：</p>\n<div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{S_0 (1-\\alpha)}{4} = \\sigma T_e^4</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:2.113em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.427em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">4</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0576em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1111em;vertical-align:-0.247em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">σ</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">4</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.247em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p>其中 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0576em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 是太阳常数，<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span></span></span></span></span> 是反照率，<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">σ</span></span></span></span></span> 是斯特藩–玻尔兹曼常数。算出的 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_e</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 约为 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mtext> </mtext><mo>∘</mo></msup><mtext>C</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-18\\ ^\\circ\\text{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">18</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mspace\"> </span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6741em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∘</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">C</span></span></span></span></span></span>——远低于实际地表平均的约 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>15</mn><msup><mtext> </mtext><mo>∘</mo></msup><mtext>C</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">15\\ ^\\circ\\text{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">15</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mspace\"> </span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6741em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∘</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">C</span></span></span></span></span></span>。这中间约 33 度的差距，全靠温室效应。</p>\n<h3 id=\"温室效应的物理本质\">温室效应的物理本质</h3><p>温室效应常被误解。它的机制其实很清楚：大气对太阳短波辐射基本透明，让阳光穿透到地表；但水汽、二氧化碳、甲烷等温室气体对地表放出的长波红外辐射有强烈吸收，吸收后又向各个方向（包括向下）再辐射。这相当于给地球盖了一层&quot;只让进、不让全出&quot;的被子，使地表温度高于单纯能量平衡的 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_e</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>。</p>\n<p>注意：温室效应本身是好事——没有它，地球会冷到不宜居。问题在于人类活动额外增加了温室气体，把这层被子加厚了，这是下一节的主题。</p>\n<h3 id=\"反馈-放大还是抑制\">反馈：放大还是抑制</h3><p>气候系统里的<strong>反馈</strong>决定了一个初始扰动最终被放大还是削弱：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>正反馈（放大）</strong>：升温→冰雪融化→反照率下降→吸收更多阳光→进一步升温（冰反照率反馈）；升温→大气能容纳更多水汽→水汽本身是强温室气体→进一步升温（水汽反馈，回到第一章的饱和水汽压随温度增大）。</li>\n<li><strong>负反馈（抑制）</strong>：升温→地表长波辐射按 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T^4</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">4</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 增强→放出更多热量→抑制升温（普朗克反馈）。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>正是这些反馈的净效果，决定了同样一份额外二氧化碳最终会带来多大的升温——这就是&quot;气候敏感度&quot;问题。</p>\n<h2 id=\"练习与思考\">练习与思考</h2><ol>\n<li>用一句话说清天气和气候的区别，并各举一个例子。</li>\n<li>简单能量平衡给出地球约 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mtext> </mtext><mo>∘</mo></msup><mtext>C</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-18\\ ^\\circ\\text{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">18</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mspace\"> </span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6741em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∘</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">C</span></span></span></span></span></span>，实际却约 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>15</mn><msup><mtext> </mtext><mo>∘</mo></msup><mtext>C</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">15\\ ^\\circ\\text{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">15</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mspace\"> </span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6741em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∘</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">C</span></span></span></span></span></span>，这 33 度的差距说明了什么？</li>\n<li>冰反照率反馈是正反馈还是负反馈？它在极地增暖中起什么作用？</li>\n<li>为什么说海洋的热惯性会让气候变化&quot;滞后&quot;？这对减排政策有什么含义？</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"拓展阅读\">拓展阅读</h2><ul>\n<li>地球辐射收支卫星观测（如 CERES）实测了进出地球的辐射，是验证能量平衡概念的直接数据。</li>\n<li>米兰科维奇循环用地球轨道参数变化解释冰期–间冰期更替，是理解自然气候变率的经典理论。</li>\n<li>&quot;气候敏感度&quot;（二氧化碳浓度翻倍对应的平衡升温）是气候科学的核心不确定性，IPCC 给出的范围值得关注，下一节会用到。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><p>这一节建立了气候的整体观：气候是大气、海洋、冰雪、陆地、生物五圈耦合的系统；全球温度由太阳短波收入与地球长波支出的能量平衡决定；温室气体对长波的吸收使地表比纯平衡温度高约 33 度；而正负反馈决定了扰动被放大还是抑制。掌握这套能量–反馈框架，你就能在下一节理解人为增暖的物理机制和未来情景。</p>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"气候系统与能量平衡","id":"气候系统与能量平衡"},{"level":2,"text":"知识要点","id":"知识要点"},{"level":2,"text":"详细讲解","id":"详细讲解"},{"level":3,"text":"气候不只是大气","id":"气候不只是大气"},{"level":3,"text":"地球的能量收支","id":"地球的能量收支"},{"level":3,"text":"温室效应的物理本质","id":"温室效应的物理本质"},{"level":3,"text":"反馈：放大还是抑制","id":"反馈-放大还是抑制"},{"level":2,"text":"练习与思考","id":"练习与思考"},{"level":2,"text":"拓展阅读","id":"拓展阅读"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"}],"prev":{"title":"数值天气预报与 AI 模型","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/natural-sciences/atmospheric-science/weather-systems-forecasting/numerical-weather-prediction"},"next":{"title":"全球变暖的机制与未来情景","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/natural-sciences/atmospheric-science/climate-and-climate-change/global-warming-and-projections"}}